Why India Is Becoming a Key Growth Market for Australian Businesses
Australian exports to India are growing rapidly, creating new opportunities for businesses looking to expand into the Indian market. Industrial exports to India, excluding coal, have increased significantly since 2022, highlighting the growing strength of the India-Australia business corridor.
For Australian businesses, India is moving from being just another international market to becoming an increasingly obvious choice for global business expansion.
With a population of more than 1.4 billion, an economy growing at around 6–7%, and consumers willing to try new brands when the product delivers value, India offers significant opportunities across industries.
India Is Not One Single Market
One of the biggest challenges for businesses entering India is understanding that India is not one uniform market.
Consumer behaviour can vary significantly between cities and regions. What works well in Mumbai or Delhi may not necessarily work in Mysore or Coimbatore.
Language, regional culture, local preferences, purchasing behaviour and even weather can influence how consumers respond to a product or service.
For businesses planning market entry into India, understanding these regional differences is essential for building the right positioning and go-to-market strategy.
Finding the Right Market Fit in India
Entering a new market is not only about having a strong product. Businesses also need to understand where their product fits and how to take it to market.
At Devakey, we have worked with businesses across manufacturing, services, education and healthcare to develop positioning that works in India and build demand-generation strategies that can convert local audiences.
The product may already be built. The next step is identifying the right market, audience, positioning and market expansion strategy.
